  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed for services, operations, and activities that are temporarily stopped. Common in business, transportation, and technology contexts. Different from {中止|ちゅうし}, which implies cancellation.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {休止|きゅうし}{中|ちゅう} (currently suspended)\n- {一時|いちじ}{休止|きゅうし} (temporary suspension)\n- {活動|かつどう}{休止|きゅうし} (activity suspension, hiatus)\n- {休止|きゅうし}{状態|じょうたい} (suspended state)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {中止|ちゅうし}: cancellation — implies the activity is called off, not just paused\n- {停止|ていし}: stop — a broader term, can be permanent or temporary\n- {中断|ちゅうだん}: interruption — implies being cut off mid-way through",
